## 3. Phase 1 — Identity & Access Baseline (browser + PowerShell, 30 min)

Goal: know exactly *who you are* in the tenant and *what your token can do*.

### 1.1 Capture a Power BI bearer token (browser only)
1. Sign in to `https://app.powerbi.com` in a normal browser window.
2. F12 → **Network** tab → filter `api.powerbi.com` → reload the page (F5).
3. Click any request (e.g. `groups?...`) → **Request Headers** → copy the full `Authorization: Bearer eyJ…` value.
4. Tokens expire in ~60 min; re-grab on 401 responses.

Alternative (DevTools Console on the app.powerbi.com tab — copies to clipboard):
```js
copy(Object.values(sessionStorage).map(v => { try { const o = JSON.parse(v); if (o.credentialType === 'AccessToken' && /powerbi|analysis\.windows\.net/.test(o.target)) return o.secret; } catch (e) {} }).filter(Boolean)[0])
```

### 1.2 Decode the token (PowerShell)
```powershell
function Get-JWTPayload {
  param([string]$Token)
  $p = $Token.Split('.')[1].Replace('-','+').Replace('_','/')
  switch ($p.Length % 4) { 2 {$p+='=='} 3 {$p+='='} }
  [Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString([Convert]::FromBase64String($p)) | ConvertFrom-Json
}
$token = '<paste>'
$claims = Get-JWTPayload $token
$claims | Select aud, upn, tid, ver, appid
$claims.roles        # application roles assigned to YOU
$claims.wids         # Entra role template GUIDs (tenant-level admin roles)
$claims.groups       # group memberships
```
Notable `wids` value: `62e90394-69f5-4237-9190-012177145e10` = Global Administrator. Any populated `roles` on a Power BI audience token is itself a finding worth investigating.

### 1.3 Record the baseline
- License (Free / Pro / Premium Per User / Fabric) — visible in Power BI UI under your account
- Workspaces listed in the left nav + your role in each (workspace → Manage access / Access list)
- Tenant ID, your UPN, whether MFA/CA policies blocked anything interesting

**Deliverable**: token claims table + your-role-per-workspace table.

