## 4. Phase 2 — Service Enumeration via REST (PowerShell, 45 min)

Goal: map every workspace, dataset, datasource, gateway, and app your token can reach — and just as importantly, **map what returns 403** (the 200/403 pattern is your permission footprint).

```powershell
$token = '<paste>'
[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [Net.SecurityProtocolType]::Tls12   # PS 5.1
$h = @{ Authorization = "Bearer $token" }
$base = 'https://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/myorg'
```

### 2.1 Workspaces
```powershell
$groups = (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/groups" -Headers $h).value
$groups | Select-Object id, name, type, state | Format-Table -AutoSize
```

### 2.2 Per-workspace inventory (reports, dashboards, datasets, dataflows, users)
```powershell
foreach ($g in $groups) {
  "=== $($g.name)  [$($g.id)]"
  foreach ($ep in 'users','reports','dashboards','datasets','dataflows') {
    try {
      $items = (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/groups/$($g.id)/$ep" -Headers $h).value
      "  {0,-12} {1}" -f $ep, $items.Count
      $items | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8 | Out-File "pbi-$($g.id)-$ep.json" -Encoding utf8
    } catch { "  {0,-12} ERROR {1}" -f $ep, $_.Exception.Response.StatusCode.value__ }
  }
}
```
From `pbi-<id>-users.json` record every user's `groupUserAccessRight` (Admin/Member/Contributor/Viewer) — this is your over-provisioning evidence list.

### 2.3 Datasource disclosure per dataset (the money call)
```powershell
foreach ($g in $groups) {
  $datasets = (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/groups/$($g.id)/datasets" -Headers $h -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).value
  foreach ($d in $datasets) {
    try {
      (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/groups/$($g.id)/datasets/$($d.id)/datasources" -Headers $h).value |
        Select-Object datasourceType, connectionDetails, credentialType, singleSignOnType, gatewayId |
        Format-List
    } catch {}
  }
}
```
`connectionDetails` typically leaks **internal server hostnames, database names, and sometimes usernames**. Also pull `/parameters` (can contain API keys/URLs as plain text) and `/refreshes?$top=10` (refresh failures leak errors/paths).

### 2.4 Gateways (if any dataset shows a gatewayId)
```powershell
$gw = (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/gateways" -Headers $h).value
$gw | Select-Object * | Format-List
foreach ($g in $gw) {
  (Invoke-RestMethod "$base/gateways/$($g.id)/datasources" -Headers $h).value |
    Select-Object datasourceType, connectionDetails, credentialType, singleSignOnType | Format-List
}
```
Record every datasource where `credentialType` is `Basic` (username+password stored) and whether `singleSignOnType` is `Kerberos` (delegation surface).

### 2.5 Apps, all-reports, subscriptions
```powershell
(Invoke-RestMethod "$base/apps" -Headers $h).value | Select-Object id, name
(Invoke-RestMethod "$base/reports" -Headers $h).value | Select-Object id, name, webUrl, datasetId | Format-Table
# per report:
(Invoke-RestMethod "$base/groups/$gid/reports/$rid/subscriptions" -Headers $h).value
```

### 2.6 Admin-only (if your account has Fabric/Power BI admin)
```powershell
(Invoke-RestMethod "$base/admin/groups?`$top=500&`$expand=admin,users,reports,dashboards,datasets,dataflows" -Headers $h).value | Measure-Object
# Scanner API (metadata + lineage for chosen workspaces):
$body = @{ workspaces = @('<workspace-guid>'); lineage = $true; datasourceDetails = $true } | ConvertTo-Json
Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post "$base/admin/workspaces/getInfo" -Headers $h -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $body
```
Non-admins: the 403s on `/admin/*` confirm you are NOT admin — record it; if a non-admin account *succeeds* on `/admin/*`, that is an immediate Critical.

### 2.7 Fabric items (if tenant has Fabric)
Grab a token from devtools while browsing Fabric items (different audience), then `GET https://api.fabric.microsoft.com/v1/workspaces` and `/v1/workspaces/{id}/items`.

**Deliverable**: workspace/dataset/datasource/gateway inventory + the 200-vs-403 map.

