## 6. Phase 4 — Sharing & Exposure Misconfigurations (browser, 45 min)

⚠️ Only with ROE approval — these create artifacts/notifications.

| # | Test | Method | Finding if… |
|---|------|--------|-------------|
| P1 | **Publish-to-web availability** | Report → File → Embed report → *Website or portal* | A public `app.powerbi.com/view?r=…` link is generated (anonymous, no RLS). **Delete the link immediately after recording evidence.** |
| P2 | Existing publish-to-web embeds | Search engine: `site:app.powerbi.com/view` + check public sites/SharePoint | Any tenant report found publicly |
| P3 | **Share link scope** | Report → Share → inspect the dropdown | "Anyone with the link" / "People in <org> with the link" available to a low-priv user; "Allow recipients to reshare" enabled |
| P4 | **Link forwarding** | Send a specific-people link to test account B (internal) | B gains access without being on the ACL |
| P5 | **External guest sharing** | Attempt to share to an external address (if approved) | Invitation succeeds / guest can view |
| P6 | **App over-distribution** | Apps list → check audiences ("entire organization" audiences) | Org-wide app containing sensitive dashboards |
| P7 | **Subscriptions** | Report → Subscribe | Can subscribe; check whether subscription emails include full snapshots of data you can't see in the report |
| P8 | **Export/download controls** | Export data + File → Download report (.pbix) | Viewers can download .pbix of a report they only partially see → they get the *entire* dataset |
| P9 | **Tenant settings review (needs admin)** | Admin portal → Tenant settings | Record: publish-to-web mode, export/download, guest access, XMLA endpoint read-write, service principals, executeQueries API toggle, workspace creation rights |

P8 is the single most common high-impact finding: **a .pbix download by a Viewer exports the whole model, not the filtered view.**

