## 9. Severity Anchors (calibrate per client context)

| Finding | Typical severity |
|---|---|
| Publish-to-web enabled + sensitive report published | Critical |
| Gateway credential recovery / gateway host compromise path | Critical |
| Non-admin succeeding on admin APIs | Critical |
| RLS bypass via impersonation / embed token identity | High–Critical |
| Over-provisioned workspace role exposing sensitive data (Contributor+ on finance/HR) | High |
| Viewer .pbix download of partially-visible model | High |
| Datasets without RLS containing sensitive data | High |
| IDOR in PBIRS REST/URL access | High |
| Internal hostname/connection-string disclosure via datasources API | Medium (info for internal attack) |
| Over-shared org-wide links/apps | Medium |
| Export controls missing | Low–Medium |

